      "Compound Microscope Parts & Alignment: Mechanical parts (base, pillar, arm, stage, coarse and fine adjustment knobs, body tube); Optical parts (eyepiece ocular lens, revolving nosepiece carrying objective lenses: 10x low power, 40x high power, 100x oil immersion); Illumination system (substage condenser, iris diaphragm, plane-concave mirror).",
      "Numerical Aperture (NA) & Resolving Power: Resolving power limit d = \\frac{0.61 \\lambda}{\\text{NA}} where \\text{NA} = n\\sin\\alpha; oil immersion (cedarwood oil refractive index n = 1.51 matching glass) eliminates light refraction and maximizes resolution.",
      "Microtomy & Hand Section Cutting: Techniques for cutting ultrathin, uniform transverse sections (T.S.) of botanical materials using a sharp straight-edge razor; holding material between pith or potato support.",
      "Biological Fixatives & Preservatives: FAA (Formalin-Aceto-Alcohol: 5 mL formalin, 5 mL glacial acetic acid, 90 mL 70% ethyl alcohol) universally preserves plant tissue architecture by coagulating nucleoproteins.",
      "Staining Mechanisms & Differential Stains: Safranin (basic red dye staining lignified, cutinized, and suberized cell walls like xylem and sclerenchyma); Fast Green (counterstain staining cellulosic living parenchyma green); Acetocarmine (nuclear and chromatin stain).",
      "Temporary Slide Mounting Protocols: Transferring section from stain to clean glass slide; adding a single drop of dilute 50% glycerin (acts as mounting medium preventing dehydration and clearing tissue); lowering coverslip at 45° angle using a mounting needle to avoid trapping air bubbles.",
      "Calibration of Ocular Micrometer: Measuring microscopic cell dimensions; calibrating ocular reticle against stage micrometer (where 1 mm is divided into 100 divisions, so 1 division = 10 \\mu m); calculating multiplication factor for each objective lens.",
      "Herbarium Specimen Pressing & Poisoning: Botanical collection; pressing plant specimens between newsprint blotters under heavy plant press; drying; poisoning with 2% mercuric chloride (HgCl_2) to prevent insect damage; mounting on standard 29 \\times 41 cm herbarium sheets.",
      "Scientific Botanical Illustration Standards: Drawing accurate biological sketches in pencil; stippling for shading (never smudge pencil); labeling on right-hand margin with straight horizontal guide lines; calculating microscopic magnification scale.",
