      "Anatomy of Marsilea Petiole (T.S.): Circular cross-section: epidermis with stomata; hypodermal sclerenchyma; cortex with circular ring of distinct air chambers separated by single-layered trabecular septa; V-shaped or triangular central vascular bundle.",
      "Morphology and Dissection of Marsilea Sporocarp: External examination of bean-shaped woody sporocarp with dorsal raphe and teeth; cutting horizontal section (H.S.) or vertical longitudinal section (V.L.S.) to observe sori attached to gelatinous ring, each containing microsporangia with microspores and megasporangia with single megaspore.",
