      "Dissecting Stereomicroscope Operation: Incident and transmitted illumination; binocular optics providing true three-dimensional depth perception; coarse focusing for macroscopic dissection inspection (magnification 10x to 40x).",
      "Compound Microscope Care for Zoological Slides: Proper centering of light path; Kohler illumination setup; using oil immersion (100x) for blood smears and protozoan cytological slides.",
      "Dissection Pan & Wax Preparation: Preparing wax-bottom dissecting trays; melting paraffin wax mixed with carbon black; pinning specimens firmly through non-diagnostic borders without damaging internal organ systems.",
      "Temporary Staining & Vital Staining: Vital stains non-toxic to living cells: Neutral Red (stains lysosomes and vacuoles in living ciliates), Methylene Blue (stains cell membranes and nuclei), Janus Green B (specifically stains active mitochondria supravitally).",
      "Collection & Culturing of Protozoa: Preparing hay infusion cultures; incubating pond water with dried grass/hay for 5-7 days; succession of ciliates: *Colpoda* \\to *Paramecium caudatum* \\to *Vorticella*; slowing rapid ciliate movement on slide using 10% methylcellulose.",
      "Preparation of Physiological Saline: Preparing 0.9% NaCl physiological saline solution for mammalian tissues and 0.65% amphibian Ringer's solution to maintain isotonicity during live cell examination.",
      "Narcotization Techniques for Invertebrates: Relaxing muscular invertebrates prior to dissection: using menthol crystals, clove oil, 70% alcohol added drop-wise, or chloroform to prevent violent tissue contraction.",
      "Humane Treatment & Ethical Guidelines (CPCSEA): Adhering to Committee for the Purpose of Control and Supervision of Experiments on Animals guidelines; replacement of live animal dissections with digital interactive simulations and virtual models wherever prescribed.",
